Appendix D. Cosmological Reconstruction: ODE Solutions and Stability

D.1 Solution of the \Lambda Equation

The ODE for \Lambda(a) derived in §6.3 is

\frac{d\Lambda}{da} - \frac{3}{a} \Lambda = -\frac{6}{a} R(a), \qquad
R(a) \equiv \frac{8\pi G_N}{\alpha} \rho_{\rm info}(a) - X(a). \tag{D.1}

Using the integrating factor \mu(a) = \exp\left(-\int \frac{3}{a}da\right) = a^{-3}, the equation becomes

\frac{d}{da}\left( a^{-3} \Lambda \right) = -6 a^{-4} R(a).

Integrating from some a_0 to a,

a^{-3}\Lambda(a) - a_0^{-3}\Lambda(a_0) = -6 \int_{a_0}^a \frac{R(\tilde a)}{\tilde a^4} d\tilde a.

Thus

\Lambda(a) = a^3 \left[ C - 6 \int_{a_0}^a \frac{R(\tilde a)}{\tilde a^4} d\tilde a \right], \tag{D.2}

with constant C = a_0^{-3}\Lambda(a_0). Changing variable to s = S_0 a^{-3} gives \Lambda(s) explicitly.

D.2 Positivity of the Kinetic Term

The kinetic term is X(a) = \frac{8\pi G_N}{\alpha} (\rho_{\rm info} + p_{\rm info}). For the \LambdaCDM expansion, \rho_{\rm info} + p_{\rm info} = \rho_c \Omega_{c0} a^{-3} > 0 (since the cosmological constant has \rho+p=0, only the dark matter contributes). Hence X(a) \ge 0 for all a, ensuring the scalar field kinetic energy is non‑negative.

D.3 Sound Speed of the Information Fluid

The information fluid is a k‑essence field with Lagrangian \mathcal{L}_{\rm info} = \alpha \sqrt{-g} [ X - \Lambda(s) ], where X = \dot\phi^2 F(\phi). The adiabatic sound speed squared is

c_s^2 = \frac{p_{\rm info,X}}{\rho_{\rm info,X}}.

From (6.2)–(6.3), \rho_{\rm info} \propto X + \frac12(\Lambda + s\Lambda') and p_{\rm info} \propto X - \frac12(\Lambda + s\Lambda'). Since \Lambda depends only on s (and thus on a through s), its derivative with respect to X vanishes. Therefore

c_s^2 = \frac{\partial p_{\rm info}/\partial X}{\partial \rho_{\rm info}/\partial X} = \frac{1}{1} = 1,

which is the speed of light. This is the usual result for a purely kinetic k‑essence field without potential mixing. A more general model with non‑trivial F(\phi) can modify the sound speed; but even with c_s^2=1, the model is stable and causal.

